**PASS.** The current build loads and starts correctly at localhost:8000, with no loading or startup defects found. The report is in `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.qSiYJ9/report.md`.

- **What was tested:** Committed HEAD e500c44 plus the same uncommitted changes as the earlier reviews; the hash of those changes matches. The built files in `dist/` are byte-identical to the previous run's and `make -n` says nothing needs rebuilding, so I didn't rebuild.
- **Server:** Nothing was running on port 8000, so I started a server on `dist/` (PID 60911). Every file it served matched `dist/`, and all 14 requests returned 200. I stopped only that server at the end.
- **First load with the cache cleared:** All 7 files loaded with 200 and nothing failed. There were no page errors and no console errors.
- **Startup time:** The title screen appeared after 279 ms, against the 2 s limit, with correct colours.
- **Console:** The only warning was Chrome refusing to start audio before the user interacts with the page. That's normal browser behaviour, not a fault.
- **Running speed:** Over 6 s the game ran at 35.14 tics/s, within the 31.5–38.5 target. The longest pause between screen updates was 10.3 ms, so the page wasn't freezing.
- **Menu:** Escape opened and closed the menu as expected.
- **Layout:** The game kept its 16:10 shape with no scrollbars at both 1280x720 and 800x600.

**Still open:**
- **Cosmetic, coder:** For about 0.1–0.3 s before the engine starts, the tab title shows the placeholder "Doom (WASM)" and the canvas is blank. This run caught it directly at 170 ms for the first time. It doesn't block anything.
- **Tester, carried over from earlier reports and not re-checked this run:** The speed and pause checks need to allow for the ~1.1 s screen-wipe freeze. The expected results in `tests/faults.sh` are also out of date.
- **Not tested, needs a person:** Firefox, Safari, high-DPI screens, latency on a non-local connection, a real background tab, and listening to the audio.

The pass criteria were written by earlier agents and haven't been approved by you; they're the same ones previous site reviews used. I made no manual interventions and changed no source, test or build files.